    {"feature": "tumor_volume_mm3", "value": 16366, "direction": "neutral"}
  ],
  "report": "The patient is a young woman (age 32) with a hormone receptor-positive, HER2-negative tumor and a low-risk MammaPrint result. While the favorable genomic profile supports the possibility of pCR, the HR-positive/HER2-negative subtype is historically associated with lower rates of complete response to neoadjuvant therapy compared to HER2-positive or triple-negative subtypes. The tumor volume is moderate at 16,366 mm³. Based on these pretreatment characteristics, the estimated probability of achieving pathologic complete response is approximately 25%."
}
```

